  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Wascomat, Electrolux Professional, Sweden, Laundrylux</h2>
    <p>When a Wascomat goes down in an LA laundromat or OPL, the failures our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run most are the front-load and control-platform items: a door gasket on high-cycle Crossover front-loads, a door interlock, an EnvoyUltra control fault after a power event, and an inverter drive fault after an LA brownout. On coin-op units it's coin mechanism wear, and on Crossover machines running softener-heavy or high-alkaline water, drain-valve and drain-pump work. We service the full Wascomat line, Crossover 2.0 (20-100 lb), Emerald (20-40 lb), legacy Gen.6, and TD/DS dryers, on the EnvoyUltra control platform, across the six counties, with parts routing through Electrolux Professional and Laundrylux distribution. Typical work runs $180-$320 for coin mechanism service, $200-$340 for a door interlock or belt, $200-$360 for an EnvoyUltra reset and programming reload, $220-$380 for a water-inlet valve or door gasket, and $700-$1,200 for a control board. Commercial diagnostic is $120, waived with the repair, BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410).</p>
    <p>Across the Wascomat fleet our techs service in LA, the failures cluster in a consistent order. EnvoyUltra control faults lead the brand-specific list, after a power event the platform can lock out cycle start or throw a drive-communication error, and most resolve at a 60-second disconnect reset plus a programming reload, with an actual board replacement needed in only about 8-to-12% of cases. Door gaskets and door interlocks on high-cycle Crossover front-loads are next, then coin mechanism wear on vended units, water-inlet valves, and drive belts. Drain-valve and drain-pump work shows up on machines running softener-heavy water chemistries. The inverter drive and control board are the last and most expensive. The European EnvoyUltra platform is what most distinguishes a Wascomat service call from an Alliance Quantum one, so our techs work from the Electrolux Professional control architecture.</p>
    <p>Wascomat is the US-market commercial laundry brand within the Electrolux Professional family. The chassis engineering originates from Electrolux Professional Laundry in Sweden (Ljungby manufacturing), distributed and serviced in the US under the Wascomat badge through Laundrylux as the long-time US authorized distributor. This distribution arrangement gives Wascomat a distinctive LA footprint: loyal to specific operator segments, European engineering heritage in the control platform and cycle programming, and parts-supply routed through the Electrolux Professional + Laundrylux channel rather than through Alliance (Speed Queen/UniMac/Huebsch) or Dexter distribution.</p>
    <p>The practical LA laundromat operator takeaway: if your spec is Wascomat, your parts channel is Electrolux Professional + Laundrylux, common service parts (door gaskets, door switches, drain pumps, water-inlet valves, drive belts) carry 1-3 day lead time through the authorized distributor, and specialty parts for Crossover 2.0 VFD drives or EnvoyUltra control boards run 3-7 days. We stock common Wascomat service parts on the truck for single-visit resolution where model compatibility matches.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>Wascomat Commercial models we service</h2>
    <div class="model-grid">
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Crossover 2.0 washers</h3><p>20, 30, 40, 60, 80, 100 lb capacities. Coin-op + card-ready + OPL-programmable variants. Current Wascomat flagship laundromat + OPL line. Service: door gasket, door interlock, inverter drive, drain pump, EnvoyUltra control, coin mechanism on coin variants.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Crossover 2.0 dryers</h3><p>Matched dryer pairs for Crossover washer capacities. Gas or electric. Service: gas valve (gas variants), heating element (electric), blower motor, belt, door switch, lint-trap pressure sensor, EnvoyUltra control integration.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Emerald series</h3><p>Emerald 20, 30, 40 lb mid-capacity laundromat-focused washers. EnvoyUltra control platform. Common at small-to-mid laundromat installs. Service overlap with Crossover on gasket + drive + valve domain.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Gen.6 (legacy)</h3><p>Prior-generation Wascomat still running at established LA laundromats. Parts supply available through Laundrylux + Electrolux Professional distribution though some legacy parts run longer lead times (5-14 days). Service is mechanical; electronics diagnosis limited by platform age.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>TD single-pocket dryers</h3><p>Commercial single-pocket dryer family. Gas or electric. Service: standard commercial dryer domain, gas valve, ignitor, flame sensor, burner, heating element (electric), blower motor, belt, door switch, thermal protections.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>DS stack dryer</h3><p>Dryer-over-dryer stack configuration for laundromats + OPL seeking doubled dry capacity in same footprint. Service covers both pockets with shared parts + independent gas/electric circuits.</p></div>
    </div>
